hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3638","I have come to know that you observe voluntary fasts every day and spend the whole night in voluntary prayers. Do not do so; your body has a right over you, your soul has a right over you. Observe (voluntary) fasts and also leave them. Fast three days in every month, and it will be as if you have fasted the whole (i.e., the entire month). Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I submitted: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! I have the strength. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then fast according to the way of Sayyiduna Dawud (peace be upon him). Fast one day and leave one day. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I wish I had accepted the concession."
"3639","I wish I had the strength for that. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not become angry because the questioner asked about the manner of his fasting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry because the questioner asked: O Messenger of Allah, how do you fast? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that he should be asked about the manner of his fasting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) feared that if he informed him about it, he would not be able to fast in the same way, or the Prophet feared for this questioner and his Ummah that it might become obligatory upon them and they would not be able to fulfill it."
"3640","""I entered with Zaid upon 'Abdullah bin Amr and he narrated: 'The Messenger of Allah was told about my fasting, so the entered upon me and I gave him an average-sized leather pillow that was stuffed with palm fibvers. He sat in the ground with the pillow between myself and him, and said: ""Whill it not be sufficient for you to fast three days each months?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah! He said: ""O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""Eleven."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah!"" Then the Prophet said: ""There is not fast better than the fast of Dawud, half of a lifetime, fasting one day and not next."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2402)"
"3641","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast three days every month. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2450)"
"3642","I was born and on which (the Qur’an or revelation) was sent down to me. That person said: What is your opinion about a person who fasts one day and does not fast the next day? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This is the way my brother, Sayyiduna Dawud (David), peace be upon him, used to fast."
"3643","“He used to fast all of Sha’ban, until he joined it to Ramadan.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1649)"
"3644","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The gates of Paradise are opened on Mondays and Thursdays, and on every Monday and Thursday the deeds (of people) are presented (before Allah Almighty)."
"3645","""The Messenger of Allah used to fast three days in the middle of every month, and he rarely did not fast on Friday."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2368)"
"3646","I could ask her on which days the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to fast the most. Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: On Saturday and Sunday. I returned to them and informed them about this, but they did not accept my statement. They thought perhaps I had not remembered the matter correctly. They sent me again, and Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) gave the same answer. I came and informed them, so all of them themselves got up and (presented themselves before Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her). They said: We had sent this person to you regarding this issue, and he has reported that you gave this answer. Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: He has spoken the truth; the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to fast most often on Saturday and Sunday. He used to say: These two are the festival days of the polytheists (they eat and drink on these days), so I wish to act contrary to them."
"3647","I asked ʿAisha, mother of the believers, ""O mother of the believers! How were the deeds of the Prophet? Did he use to do extra deeds of worship on special days?"" She said, ""No, but his deeds were regular and constant, and who among you is able to do what the Prophet ﷺ was able to do (i.e. in worshipping Allah)?"" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6466)"
"3648","Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast till one would say that he would never stop fasting, and he would abandon fasting till one would say that he would never fast. I never saw Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasting for a whole month except the month of Ramadan, and did not see him fasting in any month more than in the month of Sha'ban. (Using translation from Bukhārī 1969)"
"3649","The best fasts are three days of every month."
"3650","""A Bedouin came to the Prophet with a rabbit that he had grilled it and placed it in front of him. The Messenger of Allah refrained from eating, but he told the people to eat. The Bedouin also refrained, and the Prophet said to him: 'What is keeping you from eating?' He said: 'I fast three days of the month.' He said: 'If you was to fast, fast the shining days.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2421)"
"3651","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to command the fasting of the bright days. He used to say: This is equivalent to fasting all the time (i.e., it is equivalent to fasting the whole month). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The narrator named Minhal is the son of Milhan Qaisi. He is a companion of the Messenger. Among the companions, no one else is named Minhal."
"3652","narrates from his father that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Fasting three days in every month is equivalent to fasting the whole month and performing its voluntary acts."
"3653","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) passed his blessed hand over his head. He narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Fasting three days in every month is equivalent to fasting and breaking the fast for the whole month (here, the narrator may have misunderstood a word). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): Waki’ has narrated from Shu’bah in this narration the words “and not fasting it,” while Yahya Qattan has narrated from Shu’bah: “standing in prayer for it,” and both of these individuals are reliable and precise."
"3654","""I heard Mu'adhah saying to Aishah: 'Did the Messenger of Allah fast three days of every month?' She replied in the affirmative. So she said: 'Which of them would he fast?' She said: 'Which of them he would fast was not noticeable.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 763)"
"3655","""The Messenger of Allah used to command us to fast the three days with the shining bright nights (Al-Ayam Al-Bid), the thirteenth, fourteenth and fifteenth."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2432)"
"3656","""The Messenger of Allah commanded us to fast the three days of Al-Bid, the thirteenth, fourteenth and fifteenth."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2422)"
"3657","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast three days of each month.” I said: “Which were they?” She said: “He did not care which days they were.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1709)"
"3658","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast three days in a month and you will get the reward for the rest. I said: I have the strength for more than that. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved way of fasting to Allah is the way of Sayyiduna Dawud (peace be upon him); he would fast one day and not fast the next day. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ""Fast one day in a month and you will get the reward for the rest,"" means: you will get the reward for what remains out of the thirty days, and their ruling will be the same in this way, because it is not possible that as a person's effort increases, his reward decreases accordingly."
"3659","I am fasting. When the people finished eating, Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) came. He began to eat. The people sent their messenger towards him. He said: Why are you looking at me? By Allah! He had told me that he was fasting. So Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He spoke the truth. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever fasts three days in every month, it is as if he has fasted the whole month."" So I fast three days every month, thus it is as if I fast the whole month, and I have found confirmation of this in the Book of Allah, the Exalted (the statement of Allah, the Exalted): ""Whoever brings a good deed, he will have ten times the like thereof."
"3660","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will not be able to do this. Fast some days and leave some days. Sleep as well and offer voluntary prayers as well. Fast three days in every month. The reward of a good deed is tenfold, so this will be equivalent to fasting the whole month."
"3661","I came out to inform you about it, but two men were arguing with each other, so it was made to be forgotten by me. So, seek it on the ninth, seventh, and fifth nights. The narrator says: I said: O (Sayyiduna) Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him)! You know better than us about the counting. What is meant by the ninth, seventh, and fifth nights? He said: When it is the twenty-first night, then leave one night, then the next night will be the seventh, then leave one night, then the next will be the fifth. The narrator named Jariri says: With another chain, this is also narrated: Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said these words: ""On the third night."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The command to seek Laylat al-Qadr in the specified nights mentioned in this narration is a supererogatory command. And this command is given due to a reason, and that (reason) is to attain Laylat al-Qadr. So, whenever Laylat al-Qadr occurs in any of these mentioned nights, the command to seek it in the remaining nights is dropped from the person."
"3662","narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was residing, he used to observe i'tikaf during the last ten days of Ramadan, and when he was in a state of travel, then in the following year he would observe i'tikaf for twenty days."
"3663","Ibn 'Umar (Allah be pleased with both of them) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to observe i'tikaf in the last ten days of Ramadan. (Using translation from Muslim 1171a)"
"3664","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was residing (not traveling), he used to observe i'tikaf during the last ten days of Ramadan, and when he was traveling during the last ten days of Ramadan, then in the following year he would observe i'tikaf for twenty (20) days."
"3665","The Prophet ﷺ used to observe retirement (i'tikaf) to the mosque during the last ten days of Ramadan till Allah took him, and then his wives observed retirement to the mosque after his death. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2462)"
"3666","""When the Messenger of Allah wanted to perform I'tikaf, he would perform Fajr prayer and then he would enter his place of I'tikaf."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 791)"
"3667","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) granted her permission, so Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) had her tent set up. Lady Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) also asked his permission to observe i'tikaf with him. When Lady Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) saw this, she too had her tent set up; she was a woman of strong temperament. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw the tents of these women, he inquired: ""Did these women intend righteousness through this?"" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) abandoned the i'tikaf, and when the month of Ramadan had passed, he observed i'tikaf for twenty (20) days in the month of Shawwal."
"3668","I would wash it."
"3669","I would comb his hair. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would come home (only) to fulfill the need of relieving himself."
"3670","I would be in my chamber and the Prophet (peace be upon him) would be in the mosque."
"3671","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was observing I'tikaf (in the mosque), I would come to him to visit him. I had a talk with him and then stood up. I then returned and he (the Prophet) also stood up to accompany me (to my house). Her dwelling place was in the house of Usamah b. Zaid. Two men from the Ansar (helpers) passed (by him at the moment). When they saw the Prophet ﷺ, they walked quickly. The Prophet ﷺ said: Be at ease, she is Safiyyah daughter of Huyayy. They said: Be glory to Allah, Messenger of Allah! He said: Satan runs in man like blood. I feared he might inspire something in your mind, or he said: evil (the narrator doubted). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2470)"
"3672","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed I'tikaf, he would put his head near me, and I would comb it. and he entered the house only to fulfill human needs (i.e. to urinate or to relieve himself). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2467)"
"3673","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to spend the middle ten days of Ramadan in retirement and devotion (i'tikaf) in the mosque. One year he had retirement and devotion in the mosque (as usual); when the twenty-first night came, and this night when he used to come out his devotion in the mosque, he said: He who has engaged himself in devotion along with me should do so during the last ten days; I saw that night, that was caused to forget it, but I have seen myself prostrating in water and mud on the morning following (that night), so seek it in the last ten days and seek it every night with an odd number. Abu sa'id said: Rain fell that night, the mosque that was thatched building dripped, and my eyes saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the traces of water and mud, on his forehead on the morning following the twenty-first night. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1382)"
"3674","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to observe I'tikaf during the middle ten days of the month, and after the twentieth (day of the month), he would come out on the twenty-first and go back to his home, and those who were observing I'tikaf with him would go back like him. Then he stayed one month on the night when he used to go back home, and he addressed the people and enjoined upon them whatever Allah (SWT) willed. Then he said: 'I used to observe I'tikaf during these ten days, then I decided to spend the last ten days in I'tikaf. So whoever was observing I'tikaf with me, let him stay in his place of I'tikaf, for I was shown this night (Lailatul Qadr), then I was caused to forget it, so seek it during the last ten nights on the odd-numbered nights. And I saw myself prostrating in water and mud.'"" Abu Sa'eed said: ""It rained on the night of the twenty-first, and the roof of the Masjid leaked over the place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray. I looked at him when he had finished praying subh and his face was wet with water and mud."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1356)"
"3675","I have noticed that your dreams agree regarding the last seven nights, so whoever wants to search for it should search for it in the last seven nights."
"3676","The Messenger of Allahﷺ said, ""Seek out the Night of Qadr during the last ten nights of Ramadan, and if one of you weakens or becomes unable, let him not be overwhelmed by the remaining seven nights."""
"3677","The Prophet (peace be upon him) saw Layl..."
"3678","The Prophet (peace be upon him) saw Layl..."
"3679","The Prophet ﷺ came out to inform us about the Night of Qadr but two Muslims were quarreling with each other. So, the Prophet ﷺ said, ""I came out to inform you about the Night of Qadr but such-and-such persons were quarreling, so the news about it had been taken away; yet that might be for your own good, so search for it on the 29th, 27th and 25th (of Ramadan). (Using translation from Bukhārī 2023)"
"3680","The Prophet ﷺ as saying: Lailat al-qadr is the twenty-seventh night (of Ramadan) (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1386)"
"3681","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about Laylat al-Qadr. He said: Seek it in the last seven nights of Ramadan."
"3682","""Abu Hurairah told me that the Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever spends the nights of Ramadan in prayer (Qiyam) out of faith and in the hope of reward, he will be forgiven his previous sins, and whoever spends the night of Lailat Al-Qadr in prayer out of faith and in the hope of reward, he will be forgiven his previous sins.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2206)"
"3683","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, rather it will continue until the Day of Resurrection. I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Tell me, in which month does it occur? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If Allah permits, I will inform you about it. Seek it in the last ten nights, in one of the seven nights. After that, do not ask me about it. The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) became engaged in conversation with his companions. When I saw that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was engaged in conversation, I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! I implore you to tell me whether it is in one of these two weeks? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) became extremely angry with me; he had never been so angry with me before. He said: May your mother be bereaved of you! It is in the last week."
"3684","I observed i'tikaf in the first ten (nights and days) in order to seek that night (Lailat-ul-Qadr). I then observed i'tikaf in the middle ten days. Then (an angel) was sent to me and I was told that this (night) is among the last ten (nights). He who among you likes to observe i'tikaf should do so; and the people observed it along with him, and he (the Holy Prophet) said: That (Lailat-ul-Qadr) was shown to me on an odd (night) and I (saw in the dream) that I was prostrating in the morning in clay and water. So in the morning of the twenty-first night when he (the Holy Prophet) got up for dawn (prayer). there was a rainfall and the mosque dripped, and I saw clay and water. When he came out after completing the morning prayer (I saw) that his forehead and the tip of his nose had (traces) of clay and water, and that was the twenty-first night among the last ten (nights). (Using translation from Muslim 1167c)"
"3685","I performed i'tikaf in the first ten days seeking this night, then I performed i'tikaf in the middle ten days, then an angel came to me and I was informed that it is in the last ten nights, so whoever among you wishes to perform i'tikaf should do so. (The narrator says) The people performed i'tikaf with him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I saw this night, and in its morning I was prostrating in water and mud. On the morning of the twenty-first night, when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up to perform the morning prayer, it started to rain and the roof of the mosque began to leak. I saw the mud getting wet. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the morning prayer and came out, there was a mark of water and mud on his blessed forehead and blessed nose. This was the morning after the twenty-first night of the last ten days."
"3686","""My father narrated to me: 'The Night of Al-Qadr was mentioned in the presence of Abu Bakrah, so he said: ""I do not search for it due to something that I heard from the Messenger of Allah, except for during the last ten (nights); for indeed I heard him say: 'Search for it when nine remain, or; when seven remain, or; when five remain, or; during the last three nights.'"" He (Uyainah) said: ""During the twenty (nights) of Ramadan, Abu Bakrah used to perform Salat just as he performed Salat during the rest of the year. But when the (last) ten began, he would struggle (performing more Salat during the night)."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 794)"
"3687","I came to inform you about it, but two men were arguing with each other and Satan was with them, so it was made to be forgotten by me. So seek it in the seventh night or seek it in the fifth night."
"3688","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Night of Qadr was shown to me, then it was made to be forgotten by me. It is in the last ten nights. It is a pleasant and moderate night, neither very hot nor very cold, and during it the moon makes the stars feel ashamed. Its devil does not come out until its true dawn appears (that is, until the whole night passes)."
"3689","The narrator says: We said: O Abu'l-Mundhir! On what basis do you say this? He replied: Because of the sign, or the indication about which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us, that when the sun rises on that day, it has no rays."
"3690","I know that Laylat al-Qadr is the night about which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to spend in voluntary prayers, and it is the morning of the twenty-seventh night. It has a specific sign: the next day, when the sun rises in the morning, it is bright, but it has no rays; it appears as if it is a flat dish."
"3691","narrator named Zirr bin Hubaish used to observe continuous fasting until suhoor, then on the night before or after the twenty-seventh night, he climbed the minaret. He observed the rising of the sun and said: It has risen, but it had no rays until it became high."
"3692","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'The guests of Allah are three: The ghazi, the Hajj (pilgrim) and the Mu'tamir''' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2625)"
"3693","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Perform Hajj and 'Umrah consecutively, for they remove poverty and sin as the bellows removes impurity from iron and gold and silver, and Hajj Al-Mabrur brings no less a reward than Paradise.''' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2631)"
"3694","“Whoever performs Hajj to this House, and does not have sexual relations nor commit any disobedience, will go back like the day his mother bore him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2889)"
"3695","“From one ‘Umrah to another is an expiation for the sins that came in between them, and Hajj Mabrur (an accepted Hajj) brings no less a reward than Paradise.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2888)"
"3696","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'from one 'Umrah to another is an expiation for what comes in between, and Hajj al-Mabrur brings no reward less than Paradise.'''(sahih) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2629)"
"3697","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever performs seven circuits (tawaf) of the House of Allah (the Ka'bah), for every step he takes and every step he lifts, Allah Almighty, because of it, forgives his sin, records a good deed for him, and raises his rank because of it."
"3698","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Touching the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner wipes out sins."
"3699","narrates: Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). She said: Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) and his son have gone for Hajj and have left me behind, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: O Umm Sulaym! Performing Umrah in Ramadan is equal to performing Hajj."
"3700","“ ‘Umrah during Ramadan is equivalent to Hajj (i.e. in reward).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2991)"
"3701","The narrator states: The female narrator of this narration, Sayyida Umm Hakim (may Allah be pleased with her), had traveled to Bayt Al-Maqdis and had entered into the state of Ihram for Umrah from there."
"3702","""I said: 'O Messenger of allah, shall we not go out and fight in jihad with you, for I do not think there is any deed in the qur'an that is better than jihad.' He said: 'No. the best and most beautiful (type) of jihad is Hajj to the House; Hajj Al-Mabrur. ''(sahih) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2628)"
"3703","I keep a servant's body healthy and grant him abundance, and then five years pass over him and he does not come to Me, then he is deprived."
"3704","I had said yes, it would have become obligatory, and if it had become obligatory, you would not have been able to do it. Leave me with what I leave you about; for those before you were destroyed only because of their excessive (unnecessary) questioning of their prophets and their disagreements with them. When I forbid you from something, then avoid it, and when I command you to do something, then do it as much as you are able. He also mentioned that the following verse in Surah Al-Ma'idah was revealed regarding this: ""O you who believe! Do not ask about things which, if made plain to you, may cause you trouble."
"3705","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed the people and said: O people! Indeed, Allah has made Hajj obligatory upon yo"
"3706","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Hajj with his wives, he said: Indeed, this is the (only) Hajj, and then it is obligatory upon you to remain in your homes. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The wording of this narration has been used for some women, and by this is meant the wives of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and in this, certain situations are"
"3707","narrates regarding the statement of Allah Almighty: ""Disassociation is declared by Allah and His Messenger."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, states: When the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, returned from Hunayn, he performed ‘Umrah from Ji‘ranah. Then, on the occasion of that Hajj, he appointed Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, as the leader."
"3708","“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was on his she-camel, standing in Al-Hazwarah* saying: ‘By Allah, you are the best land of Allah, and the dearest of the land of Allah to me. By Allah, had I not been expelled from you I would never have left.’” *A place in Makkah. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3108)"
"3709","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about Makkah: ""How sweet of a land you are and how dear you are to me, and if it were not that my people expelled me from you, I would not have lived in other than you."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3926)"
"3710","He heard the Messenger of Allah saying: ""Indeed the Corner and the Maqam are two corundums from the corundum of Paradise. Allah removed their lights, and if their lights had not been removed then they would illuminate what is between east and the west."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 878)"
"3711","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(On the Day of Resurrection) this Black Stone will have a tongue and two lips, and on the Day of Resurrection it will bear witness with the truth regarding every person who touched it.”"
"3712","I heard Ibn ‘Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This Stone will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be given two eyes with which to see, and a tongue with which to speak, and it will bear witness for those who touched it in sincerity.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2944)"
"3713","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Hajar; if she had left it as it was, it would have become a flowing, great spring."
"3714","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""It is not permissible for any person to carry weapons in Makkah."
"3715","The narrator says:) A man from Yemen stood up whose name was Abu Shah. He said: O Messenger of Allah! Write this down for me. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Write it down for Abu Shah. Then Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Allow only the cutting of idhkhir (a type of grass), for we use it in our graveyards and in our homes. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Idhkhir (the ruling is different, i.e., its cutting is permitted)."
"3716","We have nothing except the Book of Allah, may He be exalted, and this document from the Prophet ﷺ. Madinah is a sanctuary from ʿAʿir to Thawr; whoever commits an offence in it or gives refuge to an offender, may the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people be upon him and no obligatory or nafl act of worship will be accepted from him.ʿ And he said: ʿProtection given by any Muslim is binding upon all of them. Whoever transgresses protection given by a Muslim, upon him be the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people, and Allah will not accept from him any nafl or obligatory act of worship. Whoever takes people as mawla without the permission of the ones who set him free, upon him be the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people, and Allah will not accept from him any nafl or obligatory act of worship.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 1037)"
"3717","‘Ali said “We wrote down nothing on the authority of the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ but the Qur’an and what this document contains.”. He reported the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying “ Madeenah is sacred from A’ir to Thawr so if anyone produces an innovation (in it) or gives protection to an innovator the curse of Allaah, angels and all men will fall upon him and no repentance or ransom will be accepted from him. The protection granted by Muslim is one (even if) the humblest of them grants it. So if anyone breaks a covenant made by a Muslim the curse of Allaah, angels and all men will fall upon him and no repentance or ransom will be accepted from him. If anyone attributes his manumission to people without the permission of his masters the curse of Allaah, angels and all men will fall upon him and no repentance or ransom will be accepted from him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2034)"
"3718","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying on the day of the conquest of Makkah: “From today until the Day of Judgment, no Quraishi will be killed while being bound.” On that day, among the disbelievers of Makkah, only Sayyiduna Muti’ (may Allah be pleased with him) came into the hands of the Muslims; his name was ‘Asi, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) named him Muti’."
"3719","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Kill him."
"3720","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Permission is granted for idhkhir. Now migration is no longer obligatory, but jihad and intention remain. And when you are called to go forth (for jihad), then go forth."
"3721","The Prophet ﷺ entered (Makkah) during they year of the Conquest, and upon his head was a helmet (Mighfar). It was said to him: 'Ibn Khatal is clinging to the covering of the Ka'bah.' So he said: 'Kill him.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1693)"
"3722","Jabir b. Abdullah reported that Allah's Apostle ﷺ entered on the day of Victory of Mecca wearing a black turban on his head. (Using translation from Muslim 1358b)"
"3723","I have been commanded (to migrate) to a town (Medina) which would overpower other towns. They (the people) call it Yathrib; its correct name is (in fact) Medina. It eliminates (bad) people just as a furnace removes the alloy of iron. (Using translation from Muslim 1382a)"
"3724","When Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Medina, Abu Bakr and Bilal got fever, and I went to both of them and said, ""O my father, how do you feel? O Bilal, how do you feel?"" Whenever Abu Bakr's fever got worse, he would say, ""Every man will meet his death once in one morning while he will be among his family, for death is really nearer to him than his leather shoe laces (to his feet)."" And whenever fever deserted Bilal, he would say aloud, ""Would that I know whether I shall spend a night in the valley (of Mecca) with Idhkhir and Jalil (i.e. kinds of grass) around me, and whether I shall drink one day the water of Mijannah, and whether I shall see once again the hills of Shamah and Tafil?"" Then I went to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him of that. He said, ""O Allah, make us love Medina as much as or more than we used to love Mecca, O Allah, make it healthy and bless its Sa' and Mud (i.e. measures), and take away its fever to Al-Juhfa."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3926)"
"3725",""" Messenger of Allah ﷺ cast a glance at Uhud and said: Uhud is a mountain which loves us and we love it."" (Using translation from Muslim 1393b)"
"3726","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) name Madinah Munawwarah as ""Tābah""."
"3727","“Faith will retreat to Al-Madinah as a snake retreats to its hole.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3111)"
"3728","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Verily, Belief returns and goes back to Medina as a snake returns and goes back to its hole (when in danger). (Using translation from Bukhārī 1876)"
"3729","“Faith will retreat to Al-Madinah as a snake retreats to its hole.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3111)"
"3730","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O group of Muslims! Glad tidings to you that the Dajjal will not enter it."" (The narrator says:) The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) meant Madinah Munawwarah."
"3731","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The terror of Dajjal will not enter Madinah Munawwarah. It will have seven gates, and at each gate there will be two angels appointed."
"3732","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Madinah is like a furnace; it removes impurities and refines what is pure."
"3733","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever leaves here out of aversion (the Prophet’s intention was Madinah Munawwarah), Allah Almighty will grant Madinah Munawwarah someone better than him in his place, and Madinah is better for the people, if only they knew.”"
"3734","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A time will come upon the people when a man will call his paternal cousins and close relatives, saying, 'Come towards ease, come towards ease,' whereas if they knew, Madinah would be better for them. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Whoever leaves here out of dislike, Allah the Exalted will grant (Madinah) someone better than him. Beware! Madinah is like a furnace, which removes impurities, and the Hour will not be established until Madinah expels its evil people just as a furnace removes the impurities (or rust) of iron."
"3735","narrates: A Bedouin accepted Islam at the blessed hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). That Bedouin developed a fever in Madinah. He (left Madinah and) went away, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Madinah is like a furnace; it removes impurities and refines goodness."
"3736","I have come to know that Ibn Jurayj used to say: We think that by this is meant Sayyiduna Imam Malik (may Allah be pleased with him). I mentioned this to Sufyan, so he said: A scholar is the one who fears Allah, and we do not know of anyone who fears Allah more than 'Umari; by this he meant Abdullah bin Abdulaziz."
"3737","“Whoever wishes bad upon the people of Al-Madinah, Allah will cause him to melt as salt melts in water.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3114)"
"3738","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever frightens the people of Madinah, Allah will frighten him."
"3739","I will be his intercessor on the Day of Resurrection."
"3740","I will be his 'intercessor' (the narrator is in doubt whether these are the words) 'witness'."
"3741","‘Whoever among you can die in Al-Madinah, let him do so, for I will bear witness in favor of those who die there.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3112)"
"3742","I will intercede for him (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) 'I will bear witness for him.'"
"3743","O Allah, bless us in our sa' and mud and shower with its blessings two other blessings (multiply blessings showerted upon it). (Using translation from Muslim 1374b)"
"3744","narrates: It was submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! Our (people of Madinah's) sa’ is the smallest sa’ and our mudd is the smallest mudd."" So the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Put blessing for us in our sa’ and mudd and in what is little and what is much for us, and along with this blessing, grant us two more blessings."
"3745","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""O Allah bestow your blessings on their measures, bless their Mudd and Sa."" The Prophet ﷺ meant the people of Medina. (Using translation from Bukhārī 2130)"
"3746","We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and when we were in the Harrah, at as-Suqya (a halting place between Makkah and Madinah) which belonged to Saʿd bin Abi Waqqas, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿBring me some water for wudoo’.” When he had done wudoo he stood up and turned to face the qiblah, then he said takbeer, then he said: O Allah, Ibrahim was Your slave and Your close friend; he prayed for blessing for the people of Makkah. I am Muhammad, Your slave and Your Messenger; I am praying to You for the people of Madinah - bless their mudd and saʿ [weights and measures] as You blessed the people of Makkah, double the blessing You bestowed upon the people of Makkah, a twofold blessing.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 936)"
"3747","“When the people would see the first fruit, they would bring it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would take it, he would say: ‘O Allah, bless for us our fruits, and bless for us our city, and bless for us our Saʿ and our Mudd, O Allah, verily, Ibrahim is Your worshipper and Your friend and Your Prophet, and verily I am Your slave and Your Prophet, and indeed, he (i.e., Ibrahim AS) supplicated to You for Makkah, and I supplicate to You for Al-Madinah with the like of that with which he supplicated to You for Makkah, and the like of it with it.’ He said: Then he would call the smallest young child he saw and give him that fruit. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3454)"
"3748","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) went to Baqi‘ and stayed there for as long as Allah willed. Then he returned, and Barirah arrived before him. She informed me, but I did not mention anything to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) until morning came. Then I mentioned this matter to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: “I was sent to the people of Baqi‘ so that I may supplicate for mercy for them.”"
"3749","""The columns of this Minbar of mine will be in Paradise."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 696)"
"3750","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Between my house and my pulpit there is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is on my fountain tank (i.e. Al-Kauthar)."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1196)"
"3751","If I saw deers grazing in Medina, I would not chase them, for Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""(Medina) is a sanctuary between its two mountains."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1873)"
